    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 8381e23fa214bd8d1f2685acc2998e2bfc6ad2d6 -->\n\nHead: 8381e23fa. Verdict: Ready for the maintainer to merge.\n\nI built and tested this head locally in a review worktree. GitHub reports it MERGEABLE with main.\n\nWhat looks good:\n- The rows edit only the draft params. Apply commits them through `EditOperationParams`. The test `a_typed_start_point_applies_through_the_history_and_undoes` proves undo and redo restore the point.\n- Off writes `None` (the automatic seam). On seeds the origin. The world does not change while you draw the tab.\n- Other kinds draw neither group and refuse a point by name at command creation (`crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs:49`). A tilted contour gets its own refusal text.\n- The values reach the generator: `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_start.rs:65` reads the start point. The app and motion suites pin the generator law; this PR does not change them.\n- No project-file field is new, and `edit_operation` already takes both params, so the MCP surface needs nothing here.\n- No snapshot PNG changed. No dependency, `build.rs`, `scripts/` or `.github/` change. New files carry a provenance line. No `unwrap` or `expect` outside tests. All files stay under 400 lines.\n\nResults (local, head 8381e23fa):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` (cwd `crates/ui`): 852 passed, 0 failed, 6 ignored. The 6 ignored are the release-lane snapshot tests.\n- The five pinning tests by name (`start_exit_rows::tests` x4, `every_field_lives_on_exactly_one_section`): 5 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib`: 333 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib`: 386 passed, 0 failed, 6 ignored.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --lib`: 54 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run: no file under `crates/ui/tests/` changed, so the diff touches no ui integration binary. The pixel snapshot lane is release-only.\n\nNotes (not blocking):\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/start_exit_rows.rs:62` and `:64`: the same help text draws twice in each group, once under the X row and once under the Y row. One hint per group is enough.\n- The PR uses `Refs`, so issue #1448 stays open with `in-review`. That matches its partly-shipped scope.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
